# Editor and OS noise
*.swp
*~
.DS_Store

# Nothing generated is ignored on purpose. The files Matugen rewrites
# (settings/colors.lua, waybar/colors.css, swaync/colors.css,
# rofi/colors.rasi, kitty/colors.conf, gtk-*/gtk.css, hyprlock-colors.conf)
# are COMMITTED with seed palettes, because several of them are hard
# requirements for their consumer to start at all — a missing
# waybar/colors.css stops Waybar rendering, and a missing colors.rasi makes
# rofi fail theme validation.
#
# The cost is that `git status` shows them dirty after your first wallpaper
# change. Silence that without untracking them:
#
#   git update-index --skip-worktree \
#       config/hypr/settings/colors.lua \
#       config/hypr/hyprlock-colors.conf \
#       config/waybar/colors.css \
#       config/swaync/colors.css \
#       config/rofi/colors.rasi \
#       config/kitty/colors.conf \
#       config/gtk-3.0/gtk.css \
#       config/gtk-4.0/gtk.css
#
# Undo with --no-skip-worktree when you want to commit a new seed.
